WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:05.030
Speaker 1: Paul Boyer is an Arizona state
senator who originally was supportive of the

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:10.440
Arizona recount of the 2020 election, which
we recently discussed, which is looking at

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:15.889
things like bamboo fibers on ballots in Maricopa
County.

00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:18.949
Paul Boyer was supportive of that originally.

00:00:18.949 --> 00:00:24.490
And that very same state senator now says
he regrets his support of that movement and

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:27.369
that it, quote, makes us look like idiots.

00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:33.680
It's, I guess, like a moment of clarity in
a sea of absurdity in Arizona.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.910
And of course, he's absolutely correct, but
really only at the micro level.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:42.860
And what I mean by that is that, yes, the
individuals who supported this nonsense and

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:48.500
I mean Josh Hawley in the U.S. Senate, people
like Paul Boyer in the Arizona State Senate,

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.830
the whole lot of them, they do look like idiots.

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:53.540
He's right about that.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:01:01.190
But the problem is that we as a country look
like idiots internationally, globally because

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:02.190
of these people.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:07.820
Now, the full quote from Senator Paul Boyer
is it makes us look like idiots.

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:10.960
I didn't think it would be this ridiculous.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.429
It's embarrassing to be a state senator at
this point.

00:01:15.429 --> 00:01:17.140
Now it's all great.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:19.340
Paul Boyer came to realize this.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:21.700
He's now saying it's a bad idea.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:28.440
OK, but you can't simply disown the entire
movement that you started simply because it

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.299
imploded in shame.

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:36.210
And what I mean by that is that Paul Boya
is reacting to the outcome of this movement.

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:39.720
Imagine if somehow I mean, it would have been
a tragedy nationally, but imagine if they

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:44.520
had found a way, a bogus way to change the
outcome of a state where they figured out

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:45.520
a way.

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:46.520
Wow.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.179
Even though Biden won Arizona, they figure
out some way to flip it to Donald Trump or

00:01:49.179 --> 00:01:53.109
imagine if they had been able to do it in
enough states to actually flip the election

00:01:53.109 --> 00:01:55.110
from Joe Biden to Donald Trump.

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:57.380
He wouldn't be saying that we looked like
idiots.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:03.420
He'd be saying we did something heroic, even
though the truth in either case is that Joe

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:04.990
Biden won.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:11.210
And being able to flip the results or even
trying to do so is a trash garbage movement.

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:18.060
He's trying to disown it now because it failed
and because it didn't go anywhere and because

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:22.030
it's become this national and global laughingstock.

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:28.400
And so he wants to wash his hands of it now
because it failed to to achieve excuse me,

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.880
what he wanted it to achieve, at least initially.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:38.240
And at some point, they need to accept that
they are, number one, wrong on the facts.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:42.280
And number two, they are idiots because they
fell for it.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:46.240
It's not just we ended up looking like idiots.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:51.230
And what's unsaid is in part because this
failed to do anything, it was idiotic to fall

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:52.650
for this from the beginning.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:57.440
And, you know, looking at Bambu Fiber's, yet
another conspiracy theory.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.680
So the point here is great.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.830
It's always great.

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:08.640
When someone realizes the error of their ways
or of their beliefs and they come to correct

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:16.150
that, that's one of the reasons why science
as a process is so valuable, because it contains

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:22.980
an error correcting mechanism and fixing mistakes
or finding that someone did something wrong,

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:24.120
believe something wrong.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.050
It's rewarded in science.

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:28.920
At least it should be when things go correctly.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:30.610
But it's not.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:35.260
You're instantly rehabilitated because one
time much too late.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:40.260
One seventy percent of Republicans still believe
to this day that Donald Trump actually won

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:43.230
the election and Joe Biden is not the legitimate
president.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:45.210
Now you say, oh, we look like idiots.

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:46.210
Oh, great.

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:47.430
Wow, you're back.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:48.430
You're great.

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:49.430
You're great.

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:54.240
Now, you stumbled into a fact among a sea
of trash propaganda and now you want a cookie.

00:03:54.240 --> 00:04:01.230
And this is you know, it's an important analysis
also in the context of the Liz Cheney thing.

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:06.450
The Republican Party are a bunch of hypocrites
when they say they're against canceling people.

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:11.740
And Liz Cheney says, hey, guys, Trump lost
and what he's doing is dangerous and what

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:12.870
he did is dangerous.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:13.870
You're canceled.

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:14.870
Yes, they're hypocrites.

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:19.470
Liz Cheney is correct that we have a process
in the process worked and we had an election

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:20.509
